# Hub iframe = lobby roots only

**Incident (Jul 2026):** Hub `iframeSrc` used `/play`, `/campaign`, `/rush/blitz`. On dsapatterns.io those paths are not static files → Cloudflare/SPA fallthrough served the **parent website** (cheat sheet) inside the game iframe.

## Hard rule

| Surface | Allowed `src` / `iframePath` |
|---------|--------------------------------|
| DSA `GamesSection.jsx` `iframeSrc` | `/games/<slug>/` only (Equalize: `/games/equalize/equalize.html`) |
| Ranbhoomi `EMBED_GAMES[].iframePath` | Same lobby root — never deep client routes |

```text
✅ /games/circuit-flow/
✅ /games/grid-tower-defense/
✅ /games/arrow-rush/
❌ /games/circuit-flow/play
❌ /games/grid-tower-defense/campaign
❌ /games/arrow-rush/rush/blitz
```

**First emotion** = lobby CTAs *inside* the game after lobby loads — not hub iframe deep-links.

## Contracts that must stay green

- Ranbhoomi: `tests/games/fleet-hub-fixes.test.mjs` — lobby-root only
- DSA: `tests/hub-iframe-titles.test.mjs` — forbids `/play|/rush/|/campaign` in hub iframeSrc

## Playtest / ship gate

Before claiming games hub OK: open `#games/<slug>`, assert iframe `src` is lobby root **and** iframe document is the game shell (brand in title/body), not DSA site chrome.

## Do not

- “Fix first emotion” by pointing hub iframe at `/play` or `/campaign`
- Let DSA hub tests assert deep links while Ranbhoomi asserts lobby roots
- Playtest only `/games/<slug>/` and skip hub `#games/<slug>` iframe checks
- Treat display-name direct URLs (`arrowrush`, `timetwin`, `last-line`, `sanctum-defense`) as hub `iframeSrc` — those are **aliases** (Worker `GAME_SPA_ALIASES` / Vercel 301), not lobby roots; see `game-tester` skill §2 URL contract

